    <briefdescription>
<para>Adapts a <ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_shard_r_p_c_client" kindref="compound">ShardRPCClient</ref> to the <ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_shard_r_p_c_server_1_1_request_handler" kindref="compound">ShardRPCServer::RequestHandler</ref> interface. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This allows a <ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_two_phase_commit_coordinator" kindref="compound">TwoPhaseCommitCoordinator</ref> to treat a remote shard (accessed via gRPC/HTTP through <ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_shard_r_p_c_client" kindref="compound">ShardRPCClient</ref>) identically to an in-process <ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_two_phase_commit_participant" kindref="compound">TwoPhaseCommitParticipant</ref>.</para>
<para>Thread-safe: the underlying <ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_shard_r_p_c_client" kindref="compound">ShardRPCClient</ref> handles its own locking.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Abort is treated as best-effort (always returns true even if the remote shard reports a failure), consistent with the abort semantics in the rest of the sharding layer. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
